language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Colour six countries with the fewest colours so that no two neighbouring countries share a colour.
given graph : matrix indexed by [int(1..9), int(1..2)] of int(1..6)
find colors : matrix indexed by [int(1..6)] of int(1..6)

branching on [colors]

minimising max(colors)

such that
$ neighbouring countries (each edge of the border graph) must have different colours
forAll e : int(1..9) . colors[graph[e,1]] != colors[graph[e,2]]
